<title>FINLAND: Merita ups Finnish 1997-98 growth forecasts.</title>
<headline>Merita ups Finnish 1997-98 growth forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banking group Merita Oy's economic research department on Tuesday raised its forecast for Finnish gross domestic product growth in 1997 to four percent from 3.5 percent forecast in August, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Merita also raised its 1998 growth forecast to 3.5 percent from three percent.</p>
<p>			(figures in percent)</p>
<p>				    1997    1998	1996</p>
<p> GDP				  +4    +3.5	+2.5</p>
<p> Exports			    +7	+6	  +3</p>
<p> Imports			    +7	+6	  +3</p>
<p> Private consumption	    +3	+3	+2.5</p>
<p> Investment			 +9	+8	  +5</p>
<p> Industrial production	  +6	+5	  +3</p>
<p> Trade balance (FIM bln)     +44     +47	 +46</p>
<p> Current account (FIM bln)   +21     +24	 +22</p>
<p> CPI				+1.0    +1.5	+0.6</p>
<p> Wage earnings		    +3    +3.5	  +4</p>
<p> Unemployment		   15.2    14.3	16.3</p>
<p> Central govt net</p>
<p>  borrowing need (FIM bln)  30	25	  40</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
